<%# Screen 06, deliberately not as mocked.
    The mockup shows three IAP packs and a "Get 15 credits" button. StoreKit is
    deferred, so every one of those would be a control that does nothing — worse
    than no control at all. This says the true thing instead, and points at the
    Library, which is free and full of content. The packs come back here when
    purchases land. %>
<div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-2.5 pt-1.5 pb-0.5">
  <div class="w-14 h-14 rounded-full bg-app-accent/[0.14] flex items-center justify-center">
    <%= app_icon "bolt", class: "w-[26px] h-[26px] text-app-accent", stroke: 1.2 %>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.4px]">You're out of credits</h2>

  <p class="text-app-text-2 text-sm leading-[1.45] max-w-[290px]">
    Each import uses 1 credit — that's the AI doing its magic. You started with
    <%= User::SIGNUP_CREDITS %> free credits and they're all used up. More credits are coming soon.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="flex flex-col gap-2 pt-1">
  <%= link_to "Browse the Library", app_library_path,
              class: "block text-center bg-app-accent text-app-on-accent rounded-full py-4 text-base font-bold" %>
  <p class="text-center text-app-text-3 text-xs leading-relaxed">
    Everything the community has already imported is free to learn.
  </p>
</div>
